ut we are firm friends."], "quotes": [{"text": "What was the difference? It was a contention in public.", "reference": "1611 April (first recorded performance), William Shakespeare, “The Tragedie of Cymbeline”, in Mr. William Shakespeares Comedies, Histories, & Tragedies […] (First Folio), London: […] Isaac Iaggard, and Ed[ward] Blount, published 1623, →OCLC, [Act I, scene v]:"}, {"text": "Away therefore went I with the constable, leaving the old warden and the young constable to compose their difference as they could.", "reference": "1714, Thomas Ellwood, The History of the Life of Thomas Ellwood: written by his own hand:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(countable, uncountable) Significant change in or effect on a situation or state.", "tags": ["countable", "uncountable"], "examples": ["It just won't make much difference to me.", "It just won't make much of a difference to anyone."], "quotes": [{"text": "The line of the horizon was clear and hard against the sky, and in one particular quarter it showed black against a silvery climbing phosphorescence that grew and grew. At last, over the rim of the waiting earth the moon lifted with slow majesty till it swung clear of the horizon and rode off, free of moorings; and once more they began to see surfaces—meadows wide-spread, and quiet gardens, and the river itself from bank to bank, all softly disclosed, all washed clean of mystery and terror, all radiant again as by day, but with a difference that was tremendous.", "reference": "1908 October, Kenneth Grahame, The Wind in the Willows, New York, N.Y.: Charles Scribner’s Sons, →OCLC:"}, {"text": "As she did so Fanny put down her book , stood up and stretched her arms, and at once Jessamy noticed a difference. It was the same Fanny but not the Fanny who climbed trees and tore her frock playing in the garden. It was as though a young lady film had settled over her, neatening her unruly hair, which was tied back with a large black bow, and primly composing her small mouth.", "reference": "1967, Barbara Sleigh, Jessamy, Sevenoaks, Kent: Bloomsbury, published 1993, →ISBN, page 105:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(countable) The result of a subtraction; sometimes the absolute value of this result.", "tags": ["countable"], "examples": ["The difference between 3 and 21 is 18."], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(obsolete) Choice; preference.", "tags": ["countable", "obsolete", "uncountable"], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "That now be chooseth with vile difference\n To be a beast, and lack intelligence.", "reference": "1590, Edmund Spenser, “Book II, Canto XII”, in The Faerie Queene. […], London: […] [John Wolfe] for William Ponsonbie, →OCLC:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(heraldry) An addition to a coat of arms to distinguish two people's bearings which would otherwise be the same. See augmentation and cadency.", "tags": ["countable", "uncountable"], "examples": [], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(logic) The quality or attribute which is added to those of the genus to constitute a species; a differentia.", "tags": ["countable", "uncountable"], "examples": [], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(logic circuits) A Boolean operation which is true when the two input variables are different but is otherwise false; the XOR operation ( scriptstyle A◌̅B+◌̅AB).", "tags": ["countable", "uncountable"], "examples": [], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(relational algebra) The set of elements that are in one set but not another ( scriptstyle A◌̅B).", "tags": ["countable", "relational", "uncountable"], "examples": [], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}], "synonyms": ["departure", "deviation", "divergence", "disparity", "conflict", "difference of opinion", "dispute", "dissension", "remainder", "nevermind", "difference", "differentiation", "differentness", "distinction", "distinguishedness", "nonidentity", "unidenticality", "diversity"], "antonyms": ["identity", "identicality", "identicalness", "sameness"]}, {"language": {"code": "en", "name": "English"}, "partOfSpeech": "verb", "pronunciations": [{"type": "ipa", "text": "/ˈdɪf(ə)ɹəns/", "tags": []}], "forms": [{"word": "differences", "tags": ["present", "singular", "third-person"]}, {"word": "differencing", "tags": ["participle", "present"]}, {"word": "differenced", "tags": ["participle", "past"]}, {"word": "differenced", "tags": ["past"]}], "senses": [{"definition": "(obsolete, transitive) To distinguish or differentiate.", "tags": ["obsolete", "transitive"], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "This simple spectation of the lungs is differenced from that which concomitates a pleurisy.", "reference": "1672, Gideon Harvey, Morbus Anglicus, Or, The Anatomy of Consumptions:"}, {"text": "[…] and souls, like in the mass, but differenced in themselves, with special gifts, duties and joys […]", "reference": "1901 [1839], Philip James Bailey, Festus: A Poem, London: George Routledge & Sons, page 10:"}, {"text": "In the Calais Roll the arms of William de Warren […] are differenced by the addition of a canton said to be that of Fitzalan […]", "reference": "1904, Arthur Charles Fox-Davies, The Art of Heraldry: An Encyclopædia of Armory, London: T.C. & E.C. Jack, page 344:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [{"language": {"code": "ar", "name": "Arabic"}, "word": "مَيَّزَ"}, {"language": {"code": "bg", "name": "Bulgarian"}, "word": "различавам"}, {"language": {"code": "ceb", "name": "Cebuano"}, "word": "sahin"}, {"language": {"code": "nl", "name": "Dutch"}, "word": "differentiëren"}, {"language": {"code": "nl", "name": "Dutch"}, "word": "onderscheiden"}, {"language": {"code": "fi", "name": "Finnish"}, "word": "erottaa"}, {"language": {"code": "de", "name": "German"}, "word": "differenzieren"}, {"language": {"code": "de", "name": "German"}, "word": "unterscheiden"}, {"language": {"code": "el", "name": "Greek"}, "word": "διακρίνω"}, {"language": {"code": "he", "name": "Hebrew"}, "word": "הבדיל"}, {"language": {"code": "hi", "name": "Hindi"}, "word": "अंतर करना"}, {"language": {"code": "io", "name": "Ido"}, "word": "diferar"}, {"language": {"code": "ne", "name": "Nepali"}, "word": "फरक छुट्याउनू"}, {"language": {"code": "fa", "name": "Persian"}, "word": "فرق گذاشتن"}, {"language": {"code": "pl", "name": "Polish"}, "word": "odróżniać"}, {"language": {"code": "pl", "name": "Polish"}, "word": "odróżnić"}, {"language": {"code": "pt", "name": "Portuguese"}, "word": "diferenciar"}, {"language": {"code": "sv", "name": "Swedish"}, "word": "skilja"}, {"language": {"code": "sv", "name": "Swedish"}, "word": "skilja åt"}, {"language": {"code": "zza", "name": "Zazaki"}, "word": "ferq kerden"}], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(heraldry) to modify a heraldic emblem so as to distinguish one branch of a house from another", "tags": [], "examples": [], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}], "synonyms": ["differentiate", "distinguish"], "antonyms": []}], "source": {"url": "https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/difference", "license": {"name": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/"}}}}